WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.891
Ananya wants her own DSA tutor, not someone

2
00:00:02.914 --> 00:00:06.095
else's chatbot. All it takes is one short

3
00:00:06.165 --> 00:00:07.291
Python script.

4
00:00:07.641 --> 00:00:10.439
Because every serious AI product starts the same

5
00:00:10.485 --> 00:00:12.982
way: with an API call.

6
00:00:13.332 --> 00:00:16.455
First, a virtual environment, so this project's packages

7
00:00:16.525 --> 00:00:18.301
never break her other work.

8
00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:21.205
Then two installs, and a small file called

9
00:00:21.263 --> 00:00:24.549
dot env, which holds her API key.

10
00:00:24.899 --> 00:00:28.254
The call itself is an ordinary HTTPS request.

11
00:00:28.672 --> 00:00:30.414
Her code sends a model name and a

12
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.958
list of messages.

13
00:00:32.308 --> 00:00:34.874
A system message sets the rules: you are

14
00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:38.078
a patient DSA tutor. A user message carries

15
00:00:38.125 --> 00:00:39.181
her question.

16
00:00:39.531 --> 00:00:41.389
The key rides along in a header, and

17
00:00:41.435 --> 00:00:43.246
the provider runs the model on its own

18
00:00:43.304 --> 00:00:44.407
servers.

19
00:00:44.757 --> 00:00:47.520
Back comes the answer, plus two fields beginners

20
00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:50.887
skip: the finish reason, and the usage.

21
00:00:51.237 --> 00:00:54.105
Stop means the model finished. Length means it

22
00:00:54.139 --> 00:00:56.636
was cut off. Usage counts the tokens she

23
00:00:56.694 --> 00:00:57.739
is billed for.

24
00:00:58.089 --> 00:01:00.132
For a follow-up, her code sends the whole

25
00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:02.791
list again, because the model remembers nothing between

26
00:01:02.861 --> 00:01:03.801
calls.

27
00:01:04.151 --> 00:01:06.496
One rule matters most. The key is a

28
00:01:06.554 --> 00:01:09.526
password. It lives in dot env, and dot

29
00:01:09.619 --> 00:01:12.139
env goes in git ignore.

30
00:01:12.489 --> 00:01:14.718
If it ever leaks, deleting the commit is

31
00:01:14.776 --> 00:01:17.446
not enough. Revoke the key and create a

32
00:01:17.516 --> 00:01:18.619
new one.

33
00:01:18.969 --> 00:01:21.767
So that is an API call: messages out,

34
00:01:21.883 --> 00:01:24.112
text and a token count back, and the

35
00:01:24.159 --> 00:01:26.074
key never touches your code.

36
00:01:26.424 --> 00:01:29.861
Next lesson: prompt engineering that survives production.
